 "notes": "Magistraliniai vamzdžiai, EN 10217. Value cells = theoretical weight in kg/m; label column = outside diameter in mm; wall-thickness column labels in mm, printed without trailing zero where whole (2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 11, 16). The label of the first column is printed on two lines in the header strip ('Diametras,' above 'mm.') and is given here as 'Diametras, mm.'. 21 rows x 21 columns (1 label + 20 value columns): 217 filled value cells, 203 empty. The body image has NO vertical grid lines; columns were assigned by x-position: the header labels start at x = 82 + 48*k px (k = 0..19) and every body value starts exactly 1 px to the right of one of these positions (checked for all 217 values), so the placement is unambiguous. Within each row the filled cells are contiguous. Column 1.8 is filled only for 21.3 and 26.9; column 16 only for 457 and 508. Trailing zeros kept as printed; two cells are printed with one decimal only: row 108 / column 5 = 12.7 and row 273 / column 7.1 = 46.6. No cell deviates from (D-t)*t*0.0246615 by more than 0.6 %. Largest deviations, transcribed as printed and NOT corrected: 139.7x2.9 = 9.73 (formula 9.78), 139.7x3.2 = 10.72 (10.77), 159x3.6 = 13.84 (13.80), 323.9x4.5 = 35.35 (35.45), 355.6x4.5 = 38.90 (38.96), 133x3.6 = 11.51 (11.49), 457x10 = 110.00 (110.24), 508x10 = 123.00 (122.81). Many values of the larger diameters are EN-table values rounded to one decimal and printed with a padding zero (e.g. 33.00, 41.40, 62.30, 98.70). Reading method: each cell was read visually at about 5-7x enlargement and, independently, decoded by pixel-exact glyph matching (un-antialiased bitmap font, pure black on white / light blue); both readings agree on every cell."
